<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34487" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπορ-ία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμπορος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>commerce</i> (acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1258b22
			</span></i>, of three kinds, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναυκληρία,
				φορτηγία, παράστασις</span> (qq. vv.)), mostly used of
				<i>commerce</i> or <i>trade by sea</i> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμπορος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					111
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				646
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				1166
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				127
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπορίαν ποιεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					2.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπορίας οὐκ οὔσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐὰν κατὰ θάλατταν ἡ ἐ. γένηται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					371a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἐμπορίην</span>, 
				Att.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίαν</span>, for <i>trade-purposes</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.139
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				17.4
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπορίας ἕνεκα</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κεν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ἐμπορίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					718
				</span></i>
			: pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς ἐ. τὰς
			κερδαλέως</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				594
			</span></i> (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τὰς ἐ. διατρίβειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1291a5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				56.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>a trade</i> or <i>business,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				6.63.8
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Damoch.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				22.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>errand, business</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hyps.Fr.</u>
				5.11
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Scyth.</u>
				4
			</span></i>; <i>journeying</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πενία
				ἀζημίωτος ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Secund.
				<u>Sent.</u>
				10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>merchandise</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Vect.</u>
				3.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.500
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Asclep.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὑτοῦ τὴν ἐ. ἔφασκεν εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					32.25
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τῇ ἐμπορίᾳ ἢν ἦγεν ἐν
				τῇ . . νηΐ</span> Test. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				35.23
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
